    "title": "Snowier Than Normal Winter Could Hit Denver, Las Vegas, Albuquerque and Kansas City as El Niño Flips the Script, While Chicago, New York and Minneapolis Fall Short - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Geraldine Adams ,\n1 days ago DENVER, CO: Winter 2026-27 could look very different from what many people expect. AccuWeather’s new winter forecast for October 2026 through April 2027 shows El Niño reshaping the season, with above-average snow possible across parts of the Southwest and central Plains, while many traditionally snowy cities in the North and East could end up below average. Read full article\n2",
